set.body:
Make lowered OperatorPrograms executable without putting private optimization kernels in the domain module.

linalg owns portable optimizer protocols, iteration kernels, stopping states, and numerical residual certificates. multivar compiles typed parameterizations, objectives, penalties, constraints, charts, and operators into those protocols and validates returned evidence before constructing OperatorProgramFit.

Initial capabilities:
- smooth objective plus separable proximal term;
- smooth objective plus direct projection constraint;
- linear-composite primal-dual form;
- exact null-space parameterization;
- fail-closed unsupported capability reporting.

Promote the current narrow primal-dual reference algorithm into the generic numerical boundary while retaining semantic lowering in multivar.

Acceptance:
- compiler capability matching is exhaustive and deterministic;
- unsupported combinations fail before iteration;
- numerical certificates bind to returned values and solver settings;
- no JVM-only dependency or explicit inverse enters shared code;
- JVM and Scala.js numerical law tests pass.
